---
jpsType: update
id: wordpress-multinode-fix-fastcgi-cache
name: Fix Nginx FastCGI Cache Directory
description: |
  One-shot repair for environments provisioned before v1.2.17.

  Recreates /var/cache/nginx/fastcgi on the cp node (wiped by a cp
  container redeploy, eg. a PHP engine swap, causing nginx -t to
  emerg-fail) and re-installs events.jps so the
  onAfterRedeployContainer hook that prevents a recurrence is
  registered going forward.

baseUrl: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/shaundma/wordpress-multi-node-v2/main

onInstall:
  - recreateCacheDir
  - reinstallEvents

actions:
  recreateCacheDir:
    - log: "Recreating /var/cache/nginx/fastcgi on cp"
    - cmd[cp]: |-
        mkdir -p /var/cache/nginx/fastcgi
        chown nginx:nginx /var/cache/nginx/fastcgi
        chmod 755 /var/cache/nginx/fastcgi
        echo "Cache dir ready: $(ls -ld /var/cache/nginx/fastcgi)"

        if systemctl is-active --quiet nginx; then
          if nginx -t 2>&1; then
            systemctl reload nginx && echo "Nginx reloaded"
          else
            echo "WARNING: nginx -t failed after cache dir recreate, not reloading"
            exit 1
          fi
        else
          echo "Nginx not running, will come up clean on next start"
        fi
      user: root

  reinstallEvents:
    - log: "Re-registering events.jps so onAfterRedeployContainer hook is active"
    - install: ${baseUrl}/scripts/events.jps?_r=${fn.random}
      skipEmail: true

success: |
  **FastCGI cache directory repaired**

  - `/var/cache/nginx/fastcgi` recreated on the cp node
  - Nginx reloaded if it was running
  - `onAfterRedeployContainer[nodeGroup:cp]` event hook re-registered
    so future cp redeploys will self-heal automatically
